# What a source distribution carries: the package (src/, with tui/app.tcss),
# pyproject.toml, the README and the changelog. Enough to build the wheel and
# to say what it is.
#
# No tests. setuptools would take tests/test_*.py by itself, without what they
# import (tests/support.py, tui_support.py, fixture_world.py) and without the
# fixtures; and several suites compare the code with the checkout around it
# (the documents, the scripts, the Makefile, git). They run from a checkout.
include CHANGELOG.md
prune tests
